   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Port Alder is a beautiful city whose painted signs are far more charming than the boring printed signs found in other places.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Machines made sign painting impossible, so Port Alder passed a law requiring every new sign to be painted by hand.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Hand-painted signs once filled Port Alder but faded when machines made signs cheaply. They are returning as owners seek distinctive shops and a veteran painter trains new artists, though cost keeps the trade small.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Students in Ingrid Matsuda's class practice basic strokes for weeks and learn to mix paint and space letters properly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Hand-painted signs once filled Port Alder but faded when machines made signs cheaply. They are returning as owners seek distinctive shops and a veteran painter trains new artists, though cost keeps the trade small.$q$, $q$The summary beginning "Hand-painted signs once filled Port Alder" covers the past, the decline, the two causes of the return and the limit. The choice about a law requiring painted signs invents a law that the passage never mentions.$q$, 'draft', '039e26ac-b513-5abf-8a33-47a590660b5c')
